Clipflow System Design
Clipflow’s first release should let you take a real clipping opportunity from saved campaign → editing project → raw footage and content plan → draft → submission → recorded earnings. That workflow gives us the architecture, data model, and first build milestone.
I’m using the PRD’s release strategy for build order and the finalized feature list for detail. The feature list says Wolf, while the PRD says Whop. I’ve used Whop as the working name. Automated collection from Whop and Content Rewards depends on verified, permitted access. Manual campaign entry is part of the first build.
1. Architecture
Use a modern full-stack web framework: Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript, backed by MongoDB with Mongoose ODM, and Tailwind CSS for the desktop-first workspace. Background workers and cron routines operate via scheduled worker processes / edge functions. Private object storage (S3-compatible) holds uploaded media and documents.

