Clipflow Database and API Design
Stack · Next.js (App Router) → Mongoose / MongoDB → Tailwind CSS, with private S3-compatible object storage and scheduled worker tasks.
Scope · Solo creator workflow from campaign discovery to recorded payout. The source brief uses both Wolf and Whop. This design uses Whop, following the PRD. The feature list marks Toolkit, Learning Hub, and References as MVP, while the numbered release plan places them after core production. Build their lightweight versions in milestone 4 after the campaign-to-payout workflow. Trends, AI, and collaboration follow separately.
1. MongoDB / Mongoose Model
Use ObjectId primary keys, ISODate for timestamps and deadlines, integer milliseconds for media offsets, and string or integer cents/minor units for monetary values. Mongoose schemas provide validation, indexing, and cascade cleanup logic. All mutable models include timestamps (createdAt, updatedAt). The collections below list domain schemas in addition to those defaults. Ordinary relationships use ObjectId references with populate support.

